## Objective
- Act as the autonomous bug-bounty agent defined by `skills/AGENT.md`: find valid, reproducible, high-impact vulnerabilities in authorized scope (`data/targets.txt` = `duel.com` + operator-authorized subdomains) and report them under `result/`.
- Create two disposable test accounts on the target, inventory subdomains/routes/APIs, then test client-side and server-side issues; fall back to unauthenticated testing only if account creation proves impossible.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn`.
- Scope: `duel.com` domain-only from `data/targets.txt`; operator note explicitly authorizes enumerating/testing `*.duel.com` subdomains. No third-party hosts, sibling domains (`duel.net`, `duel.vip`, `duel.ag`, `duelnews.com`, `cprx.online`), CDNs, or Cloudflare infra.
- Safety: no destructive/DoS/brute-force/social-engineering testing; no real-money deposits or wagers; avoid setting `balance` in mass-assignment tests (test `email_verified`, `whitelisted`, `risk_factor`, `roles` first).
- `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` only accepts confirmed vulns, format per `skills/AGENT.md` Section 9. No speculative/status-code/reflected-string findings.
- Direct `curl` to `https://duel.com/api/v2/*` returns `403` Cloudflare "IP or Country challenge blocked custom page"; headless Chrome passes the challenge, so use same-origin `fetch()` via `chrome-devtools_evaluate_script` (or curl with captured cookies + matching UA).
- Headless UA (`HeadlessChrome/156`) makes Turnstile fail (`TurnstileError ... Error: 600010`, `brunhild.challenges.cloudflare.com` `ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED`). Overriding UA to `Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/156.0.0.0 Safari/537.36` makes registration succeed.
- Registration: `POST /api/v2/auth/register`, JSON body includes `username`, `password`, `email`, `tos_agreed:true`, `tos_version:"1-20261006"`, optional `referral_code`, `seon_session_id`, and required `turnstile_token`. Direct POST without token returns `400`.
- Main API base: `/api/v2`; main SPA bundle `/assets/index-B32rJh54.js`; Vue 3 + Vite app.
- Test accounts:
  - A: `dtestqa7412` / `T3st!Passw0rd#A`, user_id `5728773`, public_uuid `PHFZEN9`, browser pageId `2`, registration reqid `736`.
  - B: `dtestqb7412` / `T3st!Passw0rd#B`, user_id `5728775`, browser pageId `3`, `isolatedContext=accountB`.
- Subdomains discovered: `www`, `pvp`, `uat-us-pvp`, `sp` (public S3-style bucket `duel-snowplow-js`), `sports-proxy` (403 JSON), `clips` (403 XML), `roulette` (404), `avatars` (401), `jobs`, `snowplow-collector`, `track.mail`; `staging`/`uat`/`dev` behind Cloudflare Access; `clips.staging` resolves but untested.
- `pvp.duel.com` loads but shows "Invalid Session — This game must be launched from the casino platform" without a casino launch token.
