## Objective
- Continue authorized security testing of `duel.com` and subdomains, focusing on PvP session/authorization flaws, without disrupting real users.

## Important Details
- Scope is `duel.com` plus its subdomains only. Third-party AWS/S3 buckets referenced by CSP are out of scope.
- Avoid affecting real users: no chat injection, no actions against live games. Use controlled accounts A/B/C and 0-balance/demo lobbies.
- Account A: `dtestqa7412`, logged in on page 2, `$0.00`.
- Account C: `dtestqc7412`, logged in on page 3 with `isolatedContext=accountB`.
- PvP iframe URL pattern exposes `session`, `st`, `game`, `return_url`; `st` is the socket secret.
- PvP session store is in `/tmp/uat_helper.js`; reads `session`, `st`, `game`, `pod`, `playerId`, `playerName`, `playerAvatar`, `balance`, `currency`, `code`/`join_code`, `replay`, `return_url`.
- Socket.io connects same-origin with `auth:{sessionId,socketSecret,device,gpu}` using `transports:['websocket']`.
- Extracted socket events include: `check-active-game`, `resume-spectate`, `join-game`, `create-game`, `create-solo-game`, `stop-solo-game`, `cancel-waiting-game`, `update-game-private`, `extend-lobby`, `negotiate-update`, `negotiate-accept`, `negotiate-exit`, `negotiate-reject`, `kick-player`, `start-game`, `leave-spectate`, `game-action`, `rematch`, `rematch-decline`, `spectate-table`, `spectate-game`, `replay-*`.
- A’s lobby session: `fc6d0f73-05ed-4ed3-a8f0-d710100563a1`, join code `C3X7P6`, creator `dtestqa7412`.
- C’s lobby session: `f8d00177-16ae-42af-8464-76ec0d6b3409`.
- Spectator session for A’s lobby: `6e99581b-8930-4b7f-9811-83f797e3977f`, `st=ee410208659808321ceb2a0e7ec7905da7c9508f2ee13b58c8ad1209ced5fe7f`, spectated game id `bb403345-1261-4037-acd2-cffd0ddf6f4b`.
- Live real game spectate code observed: `G278RM`; session `bb65d1ef-9822-4ad4-9f83-bf952670828d`. Do not send actions to this real game.
- `uat-us-pvp.duel.com` returns 200 and serves the same PvP app, but `?session=opencode-test-0001&st=opencode-test-secret` shows “Invalid session”.
- `staging`, `uat`, `dev` are behind Cloudflare Access. `jobs.duel.com` is only a mailto page. `track.mail.duel.com`, `snowplow-collector.duel.com`, `roulette.duel.com` returned 404. No dangling CNAME/takeover candidates found.

## Work State
### Completed
- Enumerated subdomains and verified Cloudflare DNS/CNAME behavior.
- Inspected PvP client bundles and identified session bootstrap, socket auth, and socket event names.
- Created controlled 0-balance PvP lobbies with A and C; obtained A join code `C3X7P6`.
- Confirmed direct access to `uat-us-pvp.duel.com` but invalid-session enforcement.
- Opening spectator session with all-zero `st` produced a socket error; caveat: duplicate-session conflict may also explain it.
- Opening spectator session directly with its correct `st` rendered as “You” creator guest lobby rather than spectator; no code shown. Not yet confirmed as a vulnerability.
- `Show code` works on A’s direct page; `Share spectate link` did not expose `st` via clipboard.

### Active
- Trying to leave/close C’s current lobby so C can join A’s lobby using code `C3X7P6`.
- Page 7 `Find Game` button is disabled because C is already a lobby creator.
- Clicked page 7 “More options”; menu was not visible in the accessibility snapshot yet.
- Alternative path: use guest/spectator session and a minimal socket.io WebSocket client to emit `join-game`/`game-action` against A’s private lobby.

### Blocked
- Cannot join with C while C is already in a lobby.
- No direct socket handle is exposed in page JS yet; may need to implement minimal Socket.IO client or inspect Vue internals.
- `Show code` intermittently does not render the code in the DOM; page 10 guest lobby has no code.
- Unclear whether all-zero `st` failure was secret validation or duplicate-session invalidation; needs a fresh spectator session retest.

## Next Move
1. On page 7, inspect the “More options” menu or DOM for a leave/cancel-waiting-lobby action and click it; then join A’s lobby with code `C3X7P6`.
2. If leaving fails, open a fresh spectator/guest session against A’s private lobby and use a minimal socket.io client to test `join-game`, spectator actions, `kick-player`, `start-game`, and bet manipulation.
3. Retest `st` validation with a fresh spectator session and a modified secret to distinguish duplicate-session failure from missing secret enforcement.

## Relevant Files
- `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/result/inventory/subdomains-hackertarget.txt`: discovered subdomain list and IPs.
- `/tmp/uat_helper.js`: PvP session store, socket auth setup, socket event names.
- `/tmp/uat_GameShell-DxrPhc1x.js`: PvP game shell; calls `initFromUrl()`, handles postMessage events.
- `/tmp/uat_GameFooterButton-CoXXw7W0.js`: lobby/footer UI logic and game code handling.
- `/tmp/uat_usePlayers-BXAjnN_l.js`: player/session UI logic.
- `/tmp/pvp_index.js` and `/tmp/uat_pvp_index.js`: identical PvP main Vue runtime bundle; dynamic game imports.
- `/tmp/uat_drift-DaTWSUz9.js`: large game chunk, not yet deeply inspected.
- `/tmp/uat_pvp.html`: UAT PvP HTML entrypoint and boot loader.
- `/tmp/jobs.html`: `jobs.duel.com` only contains a `mailto:x@duel.com` link.
- `/tmp/chunks/*.js`, `/tmp/duel_index.js`: main casino client bundles used for endpoint and Betby/proxy reconnaissance.
