- Rules: never ask user questions; test-owned data only; no real-user data; no destructive/monetary actions; if scope missing, write `result/BLOCKED.md` (not needed, scope exists).
- Session resumed after prior watchdog terminations (`status=124`); target hash preserved (`8f916756...`), run_id `40883400525`.
- Test accounts (in `result/logs/test-accounts.txt`):
  - A: username `dtestqa7412`, password `T3st!Passw0rd#A`, id `5728773`, public_uuid `PHFZEN9`, referral_code `dtestqa7412`
  - B: username `dtestqb7412`, password `T3st!Passw0rd#B`, id `5728775`, public_uuid `A2ER2K6`, referral_code `dtestqb7412`
- Login mechanics (verified working): `POST /api/v2/auth/login` body `{username, password, turnstile_token}`; Turnstile sitekey `0x4AAAAAABkme0i_7WlGNXun`, action `login`, `cData` = SHA-256 hex of username; must emulate non-headless UA `Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/156.0.0.0 Safari/537.36` or Turnstile fails (`600010`); wrong cData yields `cdata-mismatch`.
- Browser state: pageId=2 logged in as A (default context, at `https://duel.com/account`); pageId=3 logged in as B (`isolatedContext=accountB`, at `https://duel.com/`). pageId=1 is `about:blank`.
- Chrome DevTools MCP reachable at `http://127.0.0.1:9222`; `/usr/bin/google-chrome-stable` present.
- Rate limiting observed: HTTP `429` after endpoint probing; space out requests.

