## Objective
- Follow `skills/AGENT.md` exactly: autonomous, authorized bug-bounty testing of `duel.com` (scope from `data/targets.txt`), find valid reproducible high-impact vulnerabilities (XSS, CSTI, IDOR, BAC, client-side open redirect with `javascript:`), and record them under `result/`.

## Important Details
- Repo root: `/home/runner/work/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn/aaii-aautomattionn-for-doomainn`
- Scope: `duel.com` domain-only; operator note authorizes subdomain enumeration/testing of `duel.com` subdomains. No scope expansion; out-of-scope items go to `result/out-of-scope.txt`.
- Rules: never ask user questions; test-owned data only; no real-user data; no destructive/monetary actions; do not attempt to bypass security controls (e.g., spoofing `CF-Connecting-IP`/`X-Forwarded-For` to evade the country WAF).
- Test accounts (in `result/logs/test-accounts.txt`):
  - A: username `dtestqa7412`, password `T3st!Passw0rd#A`, id `5728773`, public_uuid `PHFZEN9`, referral_code `dtestqa7412`
  - B: username `dtestqb7412`, password `T3st!Passw0rd#B`, id `5728775`, public_uuid `A2ER2K6`, referral_code `dtestqb7412`
- Login mechanics: `POST /api/v2/auth/login` body `{email_or_username, password, turnstile_token}` (note server accepts `email_or_username`); Turnstile sitekey `0x4AAAAAABkme0i_7WlGNXun`, action `login`, `cData` = SHA-256 hex of username; requires non-headless UA `Mozilla/5.0 (X11; Linux x86_64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/156.0.0.0 Safari/537.36`.
- Browser state: pageId=2 logged in as A (`https://duel.com/account`, default context); pageId=3 logged in as B (`isolatedContext=accountB`, `https://duel.com/`); pageId=4 logged out (`isolatedContext=anon`); pageId=1 `about:blank`. Chrome DevTools MCP at `127.0.0.1:9222`.
- Cookie security: `duel` session cookie is SameSite=Lax (host-only) → cross-site POST CSRF not viable. `__cf_bm` uses Domain=duel.com.
- CSP on duel.com: `script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval'` + many third-party hosts; `frame-src *` → XSS impact high if any sink found.
- **WAF blocker**: all account-mutation endpoints from this IP return HTTP 403 HTML page titled `IP or Country blocked custom page`. Confirmed on `POST /api/v2/auth/password/update`, `POST /api/v2/user/username`, `POST /api/v2/referrals/set-personal-code`. Read-only GETs still work.
- Rate limits: login `x-ratelimit-limit: 10`; oauth `20` per window; `429` HTML "Rate limited" page on `/api/v2/transparency/*` after ~4 rapid requests. Space requests ≥1.5s.
- 2FA/onetime token: `POST /api/v2/user/security/token {type:'onetime'}` → 422 requiring `code`+`uuid` (2FA). Client logic: for users without `extra_security_type`, ONETIME token resolves to `''` without calling the endpoint (`NZ` fn). Email update `POST /api/v2/user/email/update {email,onetime_token,current_password}` requires real onetime token → not reachable.
- Auth chunk (re-fetched from CDN, 375 bytes) `/tmp/chunks/auth-ChFQGnu9.js` exports: `login`, `register`, `password/email`, `password/reset`, `password/update`, `attach/email {email,onetime_token,current_password}`.
- Env/config in main bundle: `VITE_PVP_ARENA_SOCKET_URL: https://pvp.duel.com`, `VITE_INTERCOM_APP_ID: lrhqdx6o`, `VITE_PAYMENTIQ_MERCHANT_ID: 100273999`, `VITE_PAYMENTIQ_TEST: 1`, `VITE_NR_BROWSER_LK: NRJS-450186af0129d0ea365`, `VITE_ENV_CLASS: main`, release `2026.43-22aa5245`.
- Prior run was terminated by watchdog (`status=124`); checkpoint results/inventory to disk continuously.

