- Inventories written: `result/inventory/routes.md`, `endpoints.md`, `javascript.md`, `result/client-side/duel.com/root/javascript/manifest.md`; `result/logs/session.md` updated.
- JS downloaded for offline analysis: `/tmp/duel_index.js` (sha256 `e6dcdc92...`), 140 chunks in `/tmp/chunks/` (`/tmp/chunks_app.txt`); also PvP app: `/tmp/pvp_index.html`, `/tmp/pvp_index.js` (131427 B), 42 chunks in `/tmp/pvp_chunks/`.
- Auth/session verified for A and B (`GET /api/v2/user` 200). Anonymous page 4 verified: `/api/v2/user`, `/user/settings`, `/user/payouts`, `/referrals/referred-users`, `/user/kyc`, `/user/intercom/credentials` all 401; `/api/v2/referrals`, `/api/v2/trade/gift-codes`, `/api/v2/user/surveys`, `/api/v2/user/security/seon-session` (GET) 404. No missing-auth found.
- `PATCH /api/v2/user` mass assignment → 405 (only GET/HEAD/DELETE).
- Referral collision: B `set-personal-code {code:"dtestqa7412"}` → 400 `"The chosen referral code is already in use by someone else."`; B restored. (Uppercase variant test blocked by 403 WAF before result.)
- IDOR/BOLA probes (B session, extra params ignored by server): `/api/v2/user/payouts?user_id=5728773` → same as self (empty); `/api/v2/referrals/referred-users?user_id=...&referral_code=...` → params ignored; `/api/v2/transparency/{username}/stats` → public stats only (all null for test accts); `/{id}/stats` → 404.
- CORS: `/api/v2/user` with `Origin: https://evil.example` → no ACAO/ACAC; `Vary: Accept-Encoding`. No CORS misconfig.
- SQLi probe `/api/v2/transparency/players?sort_column=`: `wagered` 200; `username`, `(select 1)`, `wagered,(select 1)` → 422 validation (whitelisted); then 429.
- OAuth open redirect: `GET /api/v2/oauth/login/steam` → 302 to `steamcommunity.com/openid/login` with fixed `openid.return_to=https://duel.com/api/v2/oauth/callback/steam`; `?redirect=` ignored; Google `?redirect`/`?redirect_to` ignored.
- `sp.duel.com` bucket (`duel-snowplow-js`, eu-west-1) publicly listable/readable but PUT test key `security-test-1793281639-7580.txt` → 403 AccessDenied (not writable); not referenced by main bundles.
- Avatars: `https://avatars.duel.com/avatars/e9c4b7f2a5d8624ae785fb9877248143b6ce9aee.png` → 200 image/png via CloudFront, SSE AES256.
- Static sink review: `innerHTML` only in `ChatFooter` (tiptap sanitizer, 10), `economics-changelog` (2, DOMPurify `sanitize(parse(markdown))` of server content), `cross-road`/`useSPInstance`/`sdk` (third-party). Usernames rendered via Vue text interpolation in profile/leaderboard/chat; no `v-html` on user input found.
- Hash handlers: `#profile=` validated by regex `o$` length/pattern; `#bet` validated by `X9` (int or alnum); `#merch-transfer` uses `CreditTransferModal` with `redirectTo` fixed to `` `${q9}/checkout` `` where `q9='https://duel.shop'`.
- `ChangePassword` in `account-DqpeR7qW.js` calls auth `password/update`; only shows `current_password` when `user.has_password`.
- Public-by-design: `/api/v2/transparency/{username}/stats`, `/transparency/bets`, `/transparency/players` expose usernames + deposits/withdrawals aggregates (intentional "transparency" feature; not reported). `/api/v2/affiliate-payout/totals` anon 200 aggregate totals; `/api/v2/user/zero-edge-rakeback/status` anon 200 (enabled, limits max_bet 1000, daily 50000, used 0).
- PvP app: socket.io connects to `window.location.origin` (pvp.duel.com) with auth `{sessionId, socketSecret, device, gpu}`; session store parses query params `session`, `st`, `game`, `return_url`, `code`/`join_code`, `replay`; `returnUrl` parsed but no consumer found (not exploitable open redirect). Main app chunks `_id_-zu_9lCgl.js` and `lobby-Dm0_8o7m.js` hold arena socket/postMessage logic; feature flag `PVP_ARENA_GUEST_MODE`; supports `spectate`/`table`/`hand` query params.
- `result/confirmed-vuln.txt` contains only the template header; no confirmed vulnerabilities yet.

### Active
- Static analysis of PvP arena socket/lobby chunks (`/tmp/chunks/_id_-zu_9lCgl.js`, `/tmp/chunks/lobby-Dm0_8o7m.js`, `/tmp/pvp_chunks/*`) for guest-session acquisition, postMessage origin validation, and client-trusted state — without touching real users/games.
- Read-only enumeration of remaining GET endpoints for BOLA/data exposure (leaderboard, transparency/bets, store, metadata, games, economics-changelog, careers, match-betting/betby).
- Considering read-only subdomain probes within scope: `clips.duel.com`, `track.mail.duel.com`, `sports-proxy.duel.com` (no third-party data access).

### Blocked
- All state-changing account endpoints return 403 `IP or Country blocked custom page` from this IP → stored XSS via username/avatar, password-change-without-current-password, email-update, referral case-collision tests are not executable. No control-bypass attempts allowed.
- HTTP 429 rate limiting on rapid probing; must pace requests.
- Watchdog terminations previously occurred; persist findings frequently.
- No confirmed vulnerability found so far; `result/findings/` empty.

## Next Move
1. Continue read-only testing on B (pageId=3) and anon (pageId=4) at ≥1.5s spacing: `GET /api/v2/leaderboard`, `/api/v2/transparency/bets` with filters, `/api/v2/store`, `/api/v2/metadata`, `/api/v2/games`, `/api/v2/economics-changelog`, `/api/v2/match-betting/betby`, looking for cross-user PII or IDOR; update `result/inventory/endpoints.md` with statuses.
2. Analyze PvP arena lobby chunk to determine if a guest session/socket can be obtained without login and whether postMessage handlers validate `event.origin`; if guest socket obtainable, test only self-created solo games (no real-user interference, no join-code brute force).

## Relevant Files
- `skills/AGENT.md`: master workflow/source of truth; `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`: bug-class methodology.
